    "title": "The editor's core: edit a page in place, save a draft, publish, versions and roll back",
    "why": "decisions/0159 step 3. Staff with the new Pages: edit and Pages: publish (Founder until given to a role) see editable places outlined, with Edit: the home page under the four doors (empty until something is published, so nothing changes for visitors) and every one of our pages under its text. A panel takes sections (1 to 3 columns, a background, centred or not) of blocks (heading, text, picture, button); Save draft keeps it for the team on the real page (the preview), Publish puts it live as the next version, Versions with Roll back. Rendered on the server, structured (grid, phones one column). Pictures upload through the one uploader to the site's own store. With it, the FAQ notes the drift report (live files changed without a release show in Site health).",
